Assume that the length of Earth's equator is exactly 37650 miles and that the Earth is a perfect sphere. The town of Lena, Wisconsin, is at $45^{\circ}$ North Latitude, exactly halfway between the equator and the North Pole. What is the number of miles in the circumference of the circle on Earth parallel to the equator and through Lena, Wisconsin? Express your answer to the nearest hundred miles.  (You may use a calculator for this problem.)

[asy]
size(4.5cm,4.5cm);
draw(unitcircle);
draw((-1,0)..(0,-0.2)..(1,0));
draw((-0.95,0.05)..(0,0.2)..(0.97,0.05),1pt+dotted);
draw((-0.7,0.7)..(0,0.6)..(0.7,0.7));
draw((-0.65,0.75)..(0,0.8)..(0.66,0.75),1pt+dotted);
dot((0,0));
draw((0,0)--(1,0));
draw((0,0)--(0.7,0.7));
dot((0.7,0.7));
dot((0,0.72));
label("Lena",(0.7,0.7),ENE);
label("$45^\circ$",shift(0.3,0.1)*(0,0));
[/asy]

